# Gitea uses `tea`; GitHub uses `gh`

This repository has both a **Gitea** remote (`gitea` → `git.monsterspawned.studio`) and a **GitHub** remote (`origin` → `github.com`). Use the matching CLI for each host.

## Gitea (`gitea` remote)

- Use the **`tea`** CLI (`tea pulls`, `tea issues`, `tea repos`, …) for pull requests, issues, and other Gitea API operations.
- Prefer discovering login/repo from the local remote: `tea … --remote gitea` (or `-R gitea`).
- **Do not** use `gh` against Gitea. `gh` is GitHub-oriented (GraphQL / github.com assumptions) and is unreliable or unsupported for this Gitea host.
- Example draft PR into `development`:

```bash
tea pulls create --remote gitea --draft \
  --base development \
  --head fix/your-branch \
  --title "fix: …" \
  --description "$(cat <<'EOF'
…
EOF
)"
```

## GitHub (`origin` remote)

- Use the **`gh`** CLI for GitHub-only operations (PRs, issues, checks on `github.com`).
- Do not assume `gh` can manage the Gitea remote.

## Pushing

- `git push` uses normal git remotes (`git push gitea HEAD`).
- Push to the `gitea` remote ONLY unless the user explicitly specifies otherwise on this project.
